IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XXI -- GENERAL: NOTICES, CERTIFICATES AND
-- PROOF (ss 253 to 257). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes anyone's point of view.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE READS THE TEXT.
--   * "The time it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail" is a DATE the caller supplies: the
--     Act does not say how long the mail takes. A deemed receipt answers with that date, or with NOTHING
--     when the deeming does not apply.
--   * Section 253 speaks of a "shareholder"; the keel's `Party` has `a shareholder`. A notice to a person who
--     is neither shareholder nor director is outside section 253(1).
--   * Where evidence "in the absence of evidence to the contrary" is proof, the answer is the strength of
--     proof the Act gives, never a finding that the fact is true.

§ `Part XXI -- Notices, certificates and proof`

§§ `s 253 -- notice to directors and shareholders`

-- src:3182 | 253 (1) A notice or document required by this Act, the regulations, the articles or the by-laws to be sent to a shareholder or director of a corporation may be sent by prepaid mail addressed to, or may be delivered personally to,
-- src:3183 | (a) the shareholder at the shareholder’s latest address as shown in the records of the corporation or its transfer agent; and
-- src:3184 | (b) the director at the director’s latest address as shown in the records of the corporation or in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113.
@ref CBCA s 253(1) (src:3182-3184)
DECLARE `Way of sending a notice (s 253(1))` IS ONE OF
    `prepaid mail (s 253(1))`
    `personal delivery (s 253(1))`
    `any other way of sending (s 253(1))`

-- The two paragraphs are the two kinds of recipient. Each says "at the ... latest address as shown in the
-- records": the shareholder's in the records of the corporation or its transfer agent; the director's in the
-- records of the corporation or in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113 (another piece's).
-- src:3182 | 253 (1) A notice or document required by this Act, the regulations, the articles or the by-laws to be sent to a shareholder or director of a corporation may be sent by prepaid mail addressed to, or may be delivered personally to,
-- src:3183 | (a) the shareholder at the shareholder’s latest address as shown in the records of the corporation or its transfer agent; and
-- src:3184 | (b) the director at the director’s latest address as shown in the records of the corporation or in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113.
@ref CBCA s 253(1) (src:3182-3184)
GIVEN recipient IS A Party
      way IS A `Way of sending a notice (s 253(1))`
      `it is addressed to the shareholder at the shareholder's latest address as shown in the records of the corporation or its transfer agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is addressed to the director at the director's latest address as shown in the records of the corporation or in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: sections 106 and 113 (piece cb2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a notice or document may be sent in the way within s 253(1)` IF
        (    way EQUALS `prepaid mail (s 253(1))`
         OR  way EQUALS `personal delivery (s 253(1))`)
    AND CONSIDER recipient
        WHEN `a shareholder` THEN `it is addressed to the shareholder at the shareholder's latest address as shown in the records of the corporation or its transfer agent`
        WHEN `a director` THEN `it is addressed to the director at the director's latest address as shown in the records of the corporation or in the last notice filed under section 106 or 113`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (2): "named in a notice sent by a corporation to the Director under section 106 or 113 and filed by the
-- Director" -- all three, joined by "and" in sequence.
-- src:3186 | (2) A director named in a notice sent by a corporation to the Director under section 106 or 113 and filed by the Director is presumed for the purposes of this Act to be a director of the corporation referred to in the notice.
@ref CBCA s 253(2) (src:3186)
GIVEN `the person is named as a director in a notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was sent by a corporation to the Director under section 106 or 113` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was filed by the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is presumed to be a director of the corporation within s 253(2)` IF
        `the person is named as a director in a notice`
    AND `the notice was sent by a corporation to the Director under section 106 or 113`
    AND `the notice was filed by the Director`

-- (3): deemed receipt at "the time it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail" unless there are
-- reasonable grounds for believing the shareholder or director did not receive it at that time or at all.
-- src:3188 | (3) A notice or document sent in accordance with subsection (1) to a shareholder or director of a corporation is deemed to be received at the time it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail unless there are reasonable grounds for believing that the shareholder or director did not receive the notice or document at that time or at all.
@ref CBCA s 253(3) (src:3188)
GIVEN `the notice or document was sent in accordance with subsection 253(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      recipient IS A Party
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the recipient did not receive the notice or document at that time or at all` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the date the notice is deemed received within s 253(3)` IS
    IF     `the notice or document was sent in accordance with subsection 253(1)`
       AND (    recipient EQUALS `a shareholder`
            OR  recipient EQUALS `a director`)
       AND (NOT `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the recipient did not receive the notice or document at that time or at all`)
    THEN JUST `the date on which it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4): two consecutive returns because the shareholder cannot be found; the relief lasts until the
-- shareholder informs the corporation in writing of the new address.
-- src:3190 | (4) If a corporation sends a notice or document to a shareholder in accordance with subsection (1) and the notice or document is returned on two consecutive occasions because the shareholder cannot be found, the corporation is not required to send any further notices or documents to the shareholder until the shareholder informs the corporation in writing of the shareholder’s new address.
@ref CBCA s 253(4) (src:3190)
GIVEN `the number of consecutive occasions on which a notice or document sent in accordance with subsection 253(1) was returned because the shareholder cannot be found` IS A NUMBER
      `the shareholder has informed the corporation in writing of the shareholder's new address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation is not required to send further notices to the shareholder within s 253(4)` IF
        `the number of consecutive occasions on which a notice or document sent in accordance with subsection 253(1) was returned because the shareholder cannot be found` AT LEAST 2
    AND (NOT `the shareholder has informed the corporation in writing of the shareholder's new address`)

§§ `s 254 -- notice to and service on a corporation`

-- src:3192 | 254 A notice or document required to be sent to or served on a corporation may be sent by registered mail to the registered office of the corporation shown in the last notice filed under section 19 and, if so sent, is deemed to be received or served at the time it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail unless there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation did not receive the notice or document at that time or at all.
@ref CBCA s 254 (src:3192)
GIVEN `it is sent by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is addressed to the registered office of the corporation shown in the last notice filed under section 19` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 19 (piece cb1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a notice or document may be sent to or served on a corporation within s 254` IF
        `it is sent by registered mail`
    AND `it is addressed to the registered office of the corporation shown in the last notice filed under section 19`

-- "And, if so sent": the deeming follows only a notice sent as the section allows.
-- src:3192 | 254 A notice or document required to be sent to or served on a corporation may be sent by registered mail to the registered office of the corporation shown in the last notice filed under section 19 and, if so sent, is deemed to be received or served at the time it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail unless there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation did not receive the notice or document at that time or at all.
@ref CBCA s 254 (src:3192)
GIVEN `the notice or document was sent as section 254 allows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation did not receive the notice or document at that time or at all` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the date the notice is deemed received or served within s 254` IS
    IF     `the notice or document was sent as section 254 allows`
       AND (NOT `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation did not receive the notice or document at that time or at all`)
    THEN JUST `the date on which it would be delivered in the ordinary course of mail`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 255 -- waiver of notice`

-- "Where a notice or document is required by this Act or the regulations to be sent": the articles and
-- by-laws are not mentioned, so a notice required only by them is outside the section. The consent must
-- be in writing and the person's own.
-- src:3194 | 255 Where a notice or document is required by this Act or the regulations to be sent, the sending of the notice or document may be waived or the time for the notice or document may be waived or abridged at any time with the consent in writing of the person entitled thereto.
@ref CBCA s 255 (src:3194)
GIVEN `the notice or document is required by this Act or the regulations to be sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person entitled to the notice or document has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sending or the time may be waived or abridged within s 255` IF
        `the notice or document is required by this Act or the regulations to be sent`
    AND `the person entitled to the notice or document has consented in writing`

§§ `s 256 -- certificate of the Director`

-- src:3196 | 256 (1) Where this Act requires or authorizes the Director to issue a certificate or to certify any fact, the certificate shall be signed by the Director or by a Deputy Director authorized under section 260.
@ref CBCA s 256(1) (src:3196)
GIVEN `the certificate is signed by the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is signed by a Deputy Director authorized under section 260` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate of the Director is validly signed within s 256(1)` IF
        `the certificate is signed by the Director`
    OR  `the certificate is signed by a Deputy Director authorized under section 260`

-- The strength of proof the Act gives. "Conclusive" is stronger than "in the absence of evidence to the
-- contrary".
-- src:3198 | (2) Except in a proceeding under section 213 to dissolve a corporation, a certificate referred to in subsection (1) or a certified copy thereof, when introduced as evidence in any civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding, is conclusive proof of the facts so certified without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate.
-- src:3206 | is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof of the facts so certified without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate.
@ref CBCA s 256(2), s 257(2) (src:3198 src:3206)
DECLARE `Strength of proof given by the Act (ss 256(2), 257(2))` IS ONE OF
    `conclusive proof of the facts certified`
    `proof of the facts certified, in the absence of evidence to the contrary`
    `no proof of the facts certified by force of the Act`

-- "Except in a proceeding under section 213 to dissolve a corporation": there the section does not make the
-- certificate conclusive, which is not the same as saying it proves nothing, so the answer is that the Act
-- gives no proof by force of this subsection.
-- src:3198 | (2) Except in a proceeding under section 213 to dissolve a corporation, a certificate referred to in subsection (1) or a certified copy thereof, when introduced as evidence in any civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding, is conclusive proof of the facts so certified without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate.
@ref CBCA s 256(2) (src:3198)
GIVEN `it is a certificate referred to in subsection 256(1) or a certified copy of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is introduced as evidence in a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a proceeding under section 213 to dissolve a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Strength of proof given by the Act (ss 256(2), 257(2))`
DECIDE `the strength of proof of a certificate of the Director within s 256(2)` IS
    IF     `it is a certificate referred to in subsection 256(1) or a certified copy of it`
       AND `it is introduced as evidence in a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding`
       AND (NOT `the proceeding is a proceeding under section 213 to dissolve a corporation`)
    THEN `conclusive proof of the facts certified`
    ELSE `no proof of the facts certified by force of the Act`

§§ `s 257 -- certificate of a corporation; proof`

-- (1): a director, an officer or a transfer agent may sign; the certificate states a fact set out in one of
-- the listed records.
-- src:3200 | 257 (1) A certificate issued on behalf of a corporation stating any fact that is set out in the articles, the by-laws, a unanimous shareholder agreement, the minutes of the meetings of the directors, a committee of directors or the shareholders, or in a trust indenture or other contract to which the corporation is a party, may be signed by a director, an officer or a transfer agent of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 257(1) (src:3200)
GIVEN `the certificate states a fact that is set out in the articles, the by-laws, a unanimous shareholder agreement, the minutes of the meetings of the directors, a committee of directors or the shareholders, or in a trust indenture or other contract to which the corporation is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signer is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signer is an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signer is a transfer agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a certificate issued on behalf of a corporation may be signed by the person within s 257(1)` IF
        `the certificate states a fact that is set out in the articles, the by-laws, a unanimous shareholder agreement, the minutes of the meetings of the directors, a committee of directors or the shareholders, or in a trust indenture or other contract to which the corporation is a party`
    AND (    `the signer is a director of the corporation`
         OR  `the signer is an officer of the corporation`
         OR  `the signer is a transfer agent of the corporation`)

-- (2): when introduced as evidence in a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding, any of (a),
-- (b), (c) is proof in the absence of evidence to the contrary, without proof of the signature or official
-- character of the person appearing to have signed.
-- src:3202 | (2) When introduced as evidence in any civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding,
-- src:3203 | (a) a fact stated in a certificate referred to in subsection (1),
-- src:3204 | (b) a certified extract from a securities register of a corporation, or
-- src:3205 | (c) a certified copy of minutes or extract from minutes of a meeting of shareholders, directors or a committee of directors of a corporation,
-- src:3206 | is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof of the facts so certified without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate.
@ref CBCA s 257(2) (src:3202-3206)
GIVEN `it is a fact stated in a certificate referred to in subsection 257(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a certified extract from a securities register of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a certified copy of minutes or an extract from minutes of a meeting of shareholders, directors or a committee of directors of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is introduced as evidence in a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Strength of proof given by the Act (ss 256(2), 257(2))`
DECIDE `the strength of proof of a corporation's certificate, extract or minutes within s 257(2)` IS
    IF     (    `it is a fact stated in a certificate referred to in subsection 257(1)`
            OR  `it is a certified extract from a securities register of a corporation`
            OR  `it is a certified copy of minutes or an extract from minutes of a meeting of shareholders, directors or a committee of directors of a corporation`)
       AND `it is introduced as evidence in a civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding`
       AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)
    THEN `proof of the facts certified, in the absence of evidence to the contrary`
    ELSE `no proof of the facts certified by force of the Act`

-- (3): an entry in a securities register, or a security certificate, is proof of ownership by the person in
-- whose name the security is registered, in the absence of evidence to the contrary.
-- src:3208 | (3) An entry in a securities register of, or a security certificate issued by, a corporation is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the person in whose name the security is registered is owner of the securities described in the register or in the certificate.
@ref CBCA s 257(3) (src:3208)
GIVEN `it is an entry in a securities register of, or a security certificate issued by, a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry or certificate is proof that the registered person is the owner of the securities within s 257(3)` IF
        `it is an entry in a securities register of, or a security certificate issued by, a corporation`
    AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)
